      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I know you've confirmed it, but 4000 mg four times daily (16,000 mg/day) is a dose I can't enter in good conscience. It is well into the toxic range. Doses of 400 mg/kg or more are linked to significant toxicity, and this order works out to about 230 mg/kg/day for a 70 kg patient. I know of no indication that justifies it. It would put the patient at serious risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS effects.\n\nYou also didn't give a clinical rationale, and a typo in the order is still the most likely explanation. If this is a data-entry slip, I can enter any of these right away:\n\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n\nIf you have a reason for a dose this high, I'd suggest discussing it with pharmacy or toxicology and placing the order through the pharmacy override process. That way it gets an independent safety check before it reaches the patient."
      }
